<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en" data-theme="light">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Assets | Broken references | {{siteName}}</title>
    {{>partials/head-deps.hbs}}
    {{>partials/head-styles.hbs}}
</head>
<body>
{{>partials/header.hbs}}
<main id="main" tabindex="-1" class="container">
    <div class="page-meta">
        <h1><i class="mdi mdi-image-broken-variant" aria-hidden="true"></i> Broken asset references</h1>
        <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/f">Back to All Assets</a>
    </div>

    <p class="text-secondary">
        Files referred to from a page, fragment, infobox, scheduled draft, footer override, or
        navigation entry that no asset provides — deleted, renamed, moved to another folder or locale,
        or never uploaded. Each one renders as a broken image or a dead link for readers.
    </p>
    {{! The counterpart of /f/unused, scanning the same content through the same index. Two rules keep
        this list honest, and both matter if you change it:
        1. A reference is only broken when nothing can serve it -- the locale it binds to at serve time
           has no asset AND (with assets.localeFallback on) neither does the default locale.
        2. Plain links with no file extension are page links, not assets: a page path can never contain
           a period, so an extension-less target is a page that may simply not be written yet. Those are
           left out deliberately -- see the note below. }}
    <div class="alert alert-warning py-2">
        <i class="mdi mdi-alert-outline" aria-hidden="true"></i>
        Not everything is scanned: reference-style Markdown links, custom CSS, and injected head/body
        HTML are invisible here. Links to <em>pages</em> that don't exist aren't listed either — only
        references that must be a file. Relative references (<code>![](image.png)</code>) are checked in
        page bodies, where they resolve against the page's own path; anywhere else they're listed under
        <a href="#cant-be-checked">Should be absolute</a> below.
    </div>

    {{#hasBroken}}
        <h2>Found <span class="text-secondary fs-6">({{brokenCount}})</span></h2>
        <div class="table-responsive">
            {{! data-sort-type marks a column click-to-sort (see WkBrowserCore.enableTableSort); the
                "Referenced from" column carries none -- it holds a list, not one sortable value. }}
            <table class="table table-hover align-middle" id="brokenTable">
                <thead><tr>
                    <th data-sort-type="text">Missing file</th>
                    <th data-sort-type="text">Locale</th>
                    <th data-sort-type="number">References</th>
                    <th>Referenced from</th>
                </tr></thead>
                <tbody>
                {{#broken}}
                    <tr>
                        <td><code>{{path}}</code></td>
                        <td>{{locale}}</td>
                        <td data-sort="{{refCount}}">{{refCount}}</td>
                        <td>
                            <ul class="list-unstyled mb-0">
                            {{#sources}}
                                <li>
                                    <span class="badge text-bg-light">{{type}}</span>
                                    <a href="{{url}}">{{label}}</a>{{#hasLocale}} <span class="text-secondary">({{locale}})</span>{{/hasLocale}}
                                </li>
                            {{/sources}}
                            </ul>
                        </td>
                    </tr>
                {{/broken}}
                </tbody>
            </table>
        </div>
        <p class="text-secondary">
            To fix one, either upload a file at that exact path and locale, or edit each place listed
            and point it somewhere real.
        </p>
    {{/hasBroken}}
    {{^hasBroken}}
        <p class="text-secondary">No broken references — every file referred to from this site's content exists.</p>
    {{/hasBroken}}

    {{! Relative references written where nothing can resolve them. Not listed as "broken" because we
        can't say whether they resolve -- that's exactly the problem with them. Infobox values and
        fragments are the cases worth acting on: a fragment resolves against whichever page includes it,
        and an infobox value is rendered without the page-relative pass at all, so the browser resolves
        it one path segment higher than the same markup in the page body. }}
    {{#hasUnresolvable}}
        <h2 class="mt-5" id="cant-be-checked">Should be absolute <span class="text-secondary fs-6">({{unresolvableCount}})</span></h2>
        <p class="text-secondary">
            These are written relative to the page, but sit in content that is rendered inside many pages
            — or none in particular. Each points at a different file depending on where it appears, and
            some resolve nowhere at all, so they can't be checked above. Rewrite each as an absolute path
            starting with <code>/</code>: that binds to the page's locale and falls back to the default
            locale, so it stays correct everywhere. New infobox values are already required to be
            absolute; the rest are listed here so existing content can be brought over.
        </p>
        <div class="table-responsive">
            <table class="table table-hover align-middle" id="unresolvableTable">
                <thead><tr>
                    <th data-sort-type="text">Written as</th>
                    <th data-sort-type="text">Should be</th>
                    <th data-sort-type="number">References</th>
                    <th>Written in</th>
                </tr></thead>
                <tbody>
                {{#unresolvable}}
                    <tr>
                        <td><code>{{url}}</code></td>
                        <td>{{#suggestion}}<code>{{suggestion}}</code>{{/suggestion}}{{^suggestion}}<span class="text-secondary">—</span>{{/suggestion}}</td>
                        <td data-sort="{{refCount}}">{{refCount}}</td>
                        <td>
                            <ul class="list-unstyled mb-0">
                            {{#sources}}
                                <li>
                                    <span class="badge text-bg-light">{{type}}</span>
                                    <a href="{{url}}">{{label}}</a>{{#hasLocale}} <span class="text-secondary">({{locale}})</span>{{/hasLocale}}
                                </li>
                            {{/sources}}
                            </ul>
                        </td>
                    </tr>
                {{/unresolvable}}
                </tbody>
            </table>
        </div>
    {{/hasUnresolvable}}
</main>
<script src="/static/wk-browser.js?v={{assetVersion}}"></script>
<script>
  // Click-to-sort, and drag-to-resize on desktop (enableColumnResize no-ops on touch/narrow screens,
  // and both no-op entirely if the table isn't on the page).
  (function () {
    if (!window.WkBrowserCore) return;
    window.WkBrowserCore.ensureStyle();
    ['brokenTable', 'unresolvableTable'].forEach(function (id) {
      var table = document.getElementById(id);
      if (!table) return;
      window.WkBrowserCore.enableTableSort(table, id);
      window.WkBrowserCore.enableColumnResize(table, id);
    });
  })();
</script>
{{>partials/footer.hbs}}
{{{bodyHtml}}}</body>
</html>
